# 1986 machine ROMs
#
# Drop the machine ROM images into this directory (or point --rom at a
# directory that holds them) and the emulator loads them by name. A native
# C128DCR set uses these images:
#
#   kernal.bin   0x4000 bytes — KERNAL + EDITOR + Z80-BIOS (VICE-split)
#                 from the C128DCR ROM chip (e.g. MAME 318022-02.u34):
#                   [0x0000..0x0FFF]  EDITOR    -> $C000-$CFFF
#                   [0x1000..0x1FFF]  Z80-BIOS  -> $D000-$DFFF (CP/M)
#                   [0x2000..0x3FFF]  KERNAL    -> $E000-$FFFF
#   basic.bin    0x8000 bytes — BASIC 7.0 low + high halves
#                 from the C128DCR ROM chip (e.g. MAME 318023-02.u32):
#                   [0x0000..0x3FFF]  BASIC low -> $4000-$7FFF
#                   [0x4000..0x7FFF]  BASIC high-> $8000-$BFFF
#   chargen.bin  0x2000 bytes — C64 + native-C128 character banks (optional;
#                               legacy 0x1000-byte dumps are also accepted)
#   basic64.bin   0x2000 bytes — C64 BASIC V2 (optional development test mode;
#                               basic64.rom and basic64-901226-01.bin accepted)
#   kernal64.bin  0x2000 bytes — C64 KERNAL (optional development test mode;
#                               kernal64.rom and kernal64-901227-03.bin accepted)
#   dos1571cr.bin 0x8000 bytes — integrated 1571CR DOS ROM (optional while
#                                the physical-IEC drive backend is unfinished)
#
# These ROMs are copyright Commodore and are not redistributed here. Obtain
# them from a source you are entitled to use (for example by dumping your own
# machine or using a MAME/VICE set). The emulator runs and renders its test
# pattern without them.
#
# The Z80 BIOS is extracted from the middle 4 KiB of kernal.bin; no separate
# z80bios.bin is needed. Current status: the authentic Z80 reset path hands
# the bus to the 8502 for BASIC startup and boots CP/M system disks back on
# the Z80. See docs/Z80-CPM.md.
